  "rule": {
    "title": "There is / there are",
    "explanation": "«There is» y «there are» significan hay. Usa «there is» («there's») con una sola cosa o con incontables, y «there are» con plurales:\n- «There's a café near here.»\n- «There's some milk in the fridge.»\n- «There are two bedrooms.»\n\nLa negativa es «there isn't» / «there aren't», y en la pregunta «is» o «are» va delante de «there»:\n- «There isn't a bank in this street.»\n- «There aren't any chips.»\n- «Is there a toilet? — Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.»\n- «Are there any free tables? — Yes, there are. / No, there aren't.»\n\nPara preguntar cuántos hay:\n- «How many people are there?»\n\nOjo: no confundas «there is» (hay) con «it is» (es, está). Primero dices que algo existe y después hablas de ello:\n- «There's a new pub in Clifton. It's very nice.»\n\nEn las respuestas cortas afirmativas no se contrae (nunca «Yes, there's»).",
    "table": {
      "headers": [
        "",
        "Singular / incontable",
        "Plural"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Afirmativa",
          "There's a café.",
          "There are two cafés."
        ],
        [
          "Negativa",
          "There isn't any milk.",
          "There aren't any eggs."
        ],
        [
          "Pregunta",
          "Is there a lift?",
          "Are there any shops?"
        ],
        [
          "Respuesta corta",
          "Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.",
          "Yes, there are. / No, there aren't."
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
